<title>USA: CoreStates names Albert Mandia CFO.</title>
<headline>CoreStates names Albert Mandia CFO.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>CoreStates Financial Corp said it named Albert Mandia as chief financial officer.</p>
<p>The position had been vacant since David Sparks left the company last year, shortly after CoreStates' acquisition of Meridan Bancorp in April of 1996.</p>
<p>Sparks had been Meridian's CFO, CoreStates said.</p>
<p>Since the beginning of 1996, Mandia has held both the operating and financial responsibilities in CoreStates' QuestPoint third party processing business.</p>
